This guide walks you through installing Wazuh Manager, Indexer, and Dashboard and configuring it for the lab.

Reference: Wazuh Installation Guide

1- Update System

sudo apt update && sudo apt upgrade -y
sudo apt install curl gnupg lsb-release -y

2- Add Wazuh Repository

curl -s https://packages.wazuh.com/key/GPG-KEY-WAZUH | sudo apt-key add -
echo "deb https://packages.wazuh.com/4.x/apt/ stable main" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/wazuh.list
sudo apt update

3- Install Full Wazuh Stack (Manager + Indexer + Dashboard)

curl -sO https://packages.wazuh.com/4.7/wazuh-install.sh
sudo bash wazuh-install.sh -a -i

-a = all-in-one install
-i = ignore OS compatibility check

Wait 15–25 minutes. The installer may pause during Indexer setup do not interrupt.

4- Verify Services
Check that all components are running:

sudo systemctl status wazuh-manager
sudo systemctl status wazuh-indexer
sudo systemctl status wazuh-dashboard

All should show active (running).

5- Regenerate Indexer Passwords
After install, passwords may have changed. Run:

sudo /usr/share/wazuh-indexer/plugins/opensearch-security/tools/wazuh-passwords-tool.sh --change-all

Copy the new admin password printed (e.g., wtkdbqyM?wJAbg1p5KTY5oEOj3Bgbqh9).

6- Update Dashboard Config
Edit the dashboard config to match the new password:

sudo nano /etc/wazuh-dashboard/opensearch_dashboards.yml

Set / replace these lines:

opensearch.username: "admin"
opensearch.password: "password"

Remove any # in front of the lines and keep quotes for special characters.

Restart dashboard:

sudo systemctl restart wazuh-dashboard

7- Verify Manager API

curl -k https://127.0.0.1:55000
curl -k https://:55000

Should return API info if Manager is running.

8- Access Web Interface
Open browser:

https://
or
https://localhost

Login with:

User: admin
Password: <the new password from step 5>
